## Project structure

```
floorsight/
├── backend/
│   ├── app/
│   │   ├── main.py            FastAPI app, CORS, router registration
│   │   ├── config.py          Settings from environment
│   │   ├── database.py        Session management
│   │   ├── models.py          SQLAlchemy models
│   │   ├── schemas.py         Pydantic request and response models
│   │   ├── auth.py            Hashing and JWT
│   │   ├── deps.py            get_current_user dependency
│   │   ├── metrics.py         OEE calculation
│   │   └── routers/
│   ├── alembic/               Migrations
│   └── tests/
├── frontend/
│   └── src/
│       ├── api/client.ts      Single place that talks to the backend
│       ├── context/           Auth and simulation providers
│       ├── components/
│       └── pages/
├── sample-data/
└── docker-compose.yml
```

---

## A note on scope

This was built in a focused stretch rather than over months, and the scope reflects that. There are places where a production system would need more: proper observability, background job processing for large uploads, a real permissions model beyond single-user ownership. I have tried to be specific about those rather than leaving them implied.

What I wanted to prove to myself was that I could take a problem I understood from the plant floor and build the entire software layer around it, schema through deployment, rather than configuring somebody else's platform to approximate it. That part I am happy with.

